    46	## Amendment — allocation/count consistency leg (2026-11-16, recreation Cycle 025 Condense, pattern promotion)
    47	**The leg:** for every item whose Plan carries a schedule or allocation table, this gate prices the table's **census-anchor mapping** before Execute: each prescribed onset/duration is mapped into segment-relative time (window-start offset applied) and cross-checked against every census state the wave record names for that item. A prescribed value that contradicts a named census state at its instant (e.g. a front prescribed 8% grown at the census instant whose state reads "no territory"; arrivals prescribed complete at 11300 ms against a census anchor "crowded by ~7000 ms") is a REVISE charge, primary class **UNBOUND-SCHEDULE**. A Plan whose schedule table prints no census-anchor mapping is priced as carrying an unmapped schedule — the mapping's absence is itself the charge (the table cannot be checked, which is the defect's hiding place). Count assertions ride the same leg: a summary count in the Plan that disagrees with the table it summarizes is UNBOUND-SCHEDULE's count form (A9.3's gate side).
    48	**Forcing evidence (three instances, one class):** T153 Wave 21 (timing 45 — §2b allocation contradicted the §1c census checkpoints it claimed to rest on) · T160 Wave 22 (timing 68 — prescribed onsets 2500/3500 ms already 8.33%/45.45% grown at the 449 s/452 s census instants) · T162 Wave 22 (timing 64 — even-stepped allocation completing at 11300 ms against census anchors at ~2000/~7000 ms). For T160 and T162 the build implemented the prescribed schedule exactly (verified from this cycle's filed returns, bound in Cycle 025 RUN §9b item 2); for T153 the same compliance is attributed to the seat's Wave-21 cycle record (Cycle 024 RUN §5) and is unverified in the Wave-22 stream. In all three the defect was the Plan's, discovered by the timing lens at the cost of the item's verdict.
    49	**Before/after:** before — this gate priced parameter tables for completeness and checklists for instruments, but no leg owned schedule-vs-census consistency, so three instances across Waves 21–22 shipped census-contradicting schedules through a fired gate. After — the mapping is a named Plan product and this leg prices it at the gate, where the cure costs a table edit instead of a verdict.
